5. P1 — BUILD THE PIR REGISTER
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Goal
Create a short, prioritized list of intelligence questions that support real decisions and actions.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PIR RULE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

A PIR is not just a topic.

Too broad / not actionable

• Ransomware
• Phishing
• APT groups
• Vulnerabilities

Actionable PIR example

Which actively exploited vulnerabilities or exploit campaigns affect our internet-facing, identity, email, remote-access, cloud, or critical technologies — and what action should the responsible owner take?

PIR Formula

Decision / action needed
→ Intelligence question
→ Required EEIs
→ Collection source
→ Delivery method
→ Action owner
→ Measure of success

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
INITIAL PIR REGISTER — DRAFT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Use only three to five PIRs to start.
These are drafts until stakeholders validate them.

PIR-01 — Exploited Vulnerabilities Affecting Technologies We Use
• Intelligence question: Which actively exploited vulnerabilities or exploit campaigns affect technologies we use?
• Intel 471 GIR tags: GIR 2, GIR 5
• Primary stakeholders: Vulnerability Management, Engineering, Incident Response
• Expected action: Patch, mitigate, validate exposure, hunt

PIR-02 — Intelligence Supporting Active Incident Response
• Intelligence question: What intelligence will help IR investigate, scope, contain, and understand an active incident?
• Intel 471 GIR tags: GIR 1, GIR 3, GIR 5
• Primary stakeholders: Incident Response, SOC, Forensics
• Expected action: Investigate, hunt, contain, eradicate

PIR-03 — Phishing, Credential Theft, MFA Abuse, and Account Takeover
• Intelligence question: Are our domains, identities, users, or trusted partners being targeted through phishing, credential theft, MFA abuse, or account takeover?
• Intel 471 GIR tags: GIR 4, GIR 5
• Primary stakeholders: IAM, Email Security, Incident Response
• Expected action: Block, reset, revoke, investigate, notify

PIR-04 — Relevant Threat Behaviors and Defensive Gaps
• Intelligence question: Which threat behaviors are most relevant to our environment, and where do we have detection, logging, or control gaps?
• Intel 471 GIR tags: GIR 5
• Primary stakeholders: SOC, Incident Response, Detection Engineering
• Expected action: Hunt, tune detections, improve telemetry

PIR-05 — Third-Party, Vendor, Partner, Industry, or Regional Risk
• Intelligence question: Which third-party, vendor, partner, industry, or regional threats could materially affect us?
• Intel 471 GIR tags: GIR 3, GIR 4, GIR 6
• Primary stakeholders: Risk, Engineering, Incident Response
• Expected action: Assess trust paths, monitor, restrict access

PIR-06 — Optional: New or Unexpected Public Exposure
• Intelligence question: Are approved public assets newly exposed, unexpectedly exposed, or using high-risk technology?
• Intel 471 GIR tags: GIR 2, GIR 3
• Primary stakeholders: Engineering, Vulnerability Management, Incident Response
• Expected action: Validate ownership, remediate exposure

